{"ref":"BDB, כְּבָר","hw":"כְּבָר","html":"† I. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">כְּבָר</span></big>  <strong>adv.</strong> (late) <strong>already (</strong>freq. in Mish. and NH; 𝔗 <span dir=\"rtl\">כבר</span> (rare) Syriac <span dir=\"rtl\">ܟܒܰܪ</span> usually <em>perhaps</em>, occas. <em>already</em> (Mt 11:21 Heb 1:1); Mand. <span dir=\"rtl\">כבאר</span> <em>already</em>, Nö<sup>M. p. 202</sup>. Der. uncertain, connexion with √ <span dir=\"rtl\">כבר</span> being dub.<strong>)</strong>—<em>already</em>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 1:10\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.1.10\">Ec 1:10</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">כְּבָר הָיָה</span> it hath <em>already</em> been, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:12\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.12\">2:12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:16\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.16\">16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 3:15\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.3.15\">3:15</a><sup>(×2)</sup>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 4:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.4.2\">4:2</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 6:10\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.6.10\">6:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:6\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.6\">9:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:7\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.7\">7</a>.","next":"BDB, כְּבָר²","prev":"BDB, כִּבְרָה"}